{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do","id":1282780,"title":"Who is dis pater and what does he do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-25T20:44:33-08:00","id":1282780,"title":"Who is dis pater and what does he do?","content":"I've been trying to look into this for awhile and haven't found much outside the small section in the Gio clan book. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have any info or a place I could look to find out, who the father of wealth is, what he does, or why?<br /> <br /> Is he mentioned in Wraith at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T17:45:04-08:00","id":1282931,"title":"","content":"Dis Pater as an ancient Roman deity of the underworld and wealth - both of which interest the Giovanni. However, what Dis Pater is, at least as described by the Giovanni Clan Book) has never been specified.<br /> <br /> Edit: Assuming Dis Pater is a real wraith, then it must be a powerful inside the society of the Underworld. A likely candidate is the Smiling Lord - the nominal lord of those who die by violence - as he was always a treacherous bastard and might have thrown in with the Gs as part of a long-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 01-26-2019, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T23:04:16-08:00","id":1282968,"title":"","content":"It's Latin for 'rich father' (Father of Riches might be a little closer to the intent), a title often associated with the Roman god of the Underworld, Pluto. My impression was always that it was one of the Malfeans or its Nephwrack mouth piece, given the clan's goal of tearing down the Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T03:35:10-08:00","id":1283003,"title":"","content":"I like to think yeah Dis Pater May be a mask of a Malfean, or some other Strange Spirit with power over the Underworld and the dead. Maybe his power is in Secrets, Ancient Contracts, and Blessings and curses concerning underworld affairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T03:59:16-08:00","id":1283014,"title":"","content":"I always thought that &quot;Dis Pater&quot; was a kind of personification of the concept of death and afterlife rather than refering to any specific creature. But then again I'm not all that into either Giovanni or the Cappadocians and I know about nothing about Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T09:53:10-08:00","id":1283071,"title":"","content":"Dis Pater (&quot;The father of riches&quot;) was the roman god of death before he was subsumed into Pluto/Hades cult. In the World of Darkness he's supposed to be an extremely old and powerful wraith who acted as the Giovanni's patron at least a thousand years before Capapdocius embraced Augustus. Keep in mind that in roman times the Giovanni used to be called the Ioveanus, a family of mortal merchants/negromancers. Having someone like the &quot;Father of Riches&quot; as their patron was then completely appropriate.<br /> <br /> When he was embraced Augustus was the &quot;pater familias&quot; of the Giovanni family, one of their most powerful negromancers and he was supposedly a few centuries old due to being a mage. Given his position and sorcerous might, it stands to reason Augustus knew of Dis Pater and was in contact with him well before the embrace. If that's so, Augustus accepting Cappadocius offer could have deeper implications than most people assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T13:35:38-08:00","id":1283108,"title":"","content":"Which is what makes it all so interesting, especially playing a character that might be unwittingly working to end the world as we know it with the endless night. Which, sounds like it obviously won't work the way they think.<br /> <br /> At least the Setites know what the general plan is, whether or not it backfires.<br /> <br /> After reading here, I finally found a wikipedia and the link to death itself is mentioned, but more often mentioned is the connection to Pluto.<br /> <br /> I still wish the books gave a little more info, especially on his interactions with the hierarchy and the shadowlands in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:41:11-08:00","id":1283131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talvas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283108#post1283108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is what makes it all so interesting, especially playing a character that might be unwittingly working to end the world as we know it with the endless night. Which, sounds like it obviously won't work the way they think.<br /> <br /> At least the Setites know what the general plan is, whether or not it backfires.<br /> <br /> After reading here, I finally found a wikipedia and the link to death itself is mentioned, but more often mentioned is the connection to Pluto.<br /> <br /> I still wish the books gave a little more info, especially on his interactions with the hierarchy and the shadowlands in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind not all the Giovanni are working for the Endless Night. Augustus is, and he ultimately commands the clan, but the list of those &quot;in the known&quot; is very short indeed and a few of those are actually trying to prevent Augustus from suceeding, among them Ambrogino Giovanni. Most Giovanni ancillae and neonates don't even believe Augustus exists!<br /> Beckett's jyhad diary mentions several possible scenarios for what happens if the Endless Night ritual is successfully enacted. They vary from &quot;Augustus Wins&quot; to &quot;The Wraiths tricked the Giovanni and rule the world&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T14:34:55-08:00","id":1283568,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/XtHQKml.gif?noredirect\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Just another mask worn by Cappadocius, maybe? I like the idea the Giovanni were worshipping him even before they knew about vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T15:38:17-08:00","id":1283582,"title":"","content":"&quot;It was Me Di.. Saulot all along!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T16:01:07-08:00","id":1283588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283568#post1283568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/XtHQKml.gif?noredirect\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Just another mask worn by Cappadocius, maybe? I like the idea the Giovanni were worshipping him even before they knew about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what has he, or it, being doing the last 575 years? It does make for an interesting idea, that the Johns had been played in a very long con - and how Augustus would have reacted when he found out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T16:41:20-08:00","id":1283592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283071#post1283071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When he was embraced Augustus was the &amp;quot;pater familias&amp;quot; of the Giovanni family, one of their most powerful negromancers and he was supposedly a few centuries old due to being a mage. Given his position and sorcerous might, it stands to reason Augustus knew of Dis Pater and was in contact with him well before the embrace. If that's so, Augustus accepting Cappadocius offer could have deeper implications than most people assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... Augustus was 59-60, depending on his birthday, when he was embraced. He's young enough that his age isn't up for speculation like most 4th gens. He was born in 945, embraced in 1005.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T17:28:21-08:00","id":1283601,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Cult of Typhon, as you see, survived in a fex places, celebrating the rites of Bacchus, Pluto and Mars. Even some cult groups persisted witout any vampire to lead them. For Example, a letter from a Setite of Venice of the tenth century mentions acult of Pluto all-mortal called the Skiathos of Dis, led by a family named DiGiovanni.&quot;<br /> <br /> -Clanbook: Setite revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T19:10:35-08:00","id":1283620,"title":"","content":"The etymology of \u201cDis\u201d is hardly certain. It\u2019s probably one of many reflexes of an Indo-European word meaning \u201cdivine,\u201d but Cicero suggests it\u2019s a contraction of \u201cdives,\u201d meaning \u201crich,\u201d in order to make it a native Latin equivalent to the Greek-derived \u201cPluto.\u201d But that doesn\u2019t square with early uses in which it\u2019s a more generic divine title. <br /> <br /> In any case, regardless of origins, for the entire historical period there\u2019s no meaningful distinction between Dis Pater, Orcus, Hades, and Pluto. And Serapis, for that matter. That\u2019s how the ancestors of the Giovanni would have understood him: the lord of the underworld, who also happens to be the granter of riches. <br /> <br /> Now, what were they *really* worshiping? Well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T10:03:07-08:00","id":1283740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283588#post1283588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then what has he, or it, being doing the last 575 years? It does make for an interesting idea, that the Johns had been played in a very long con - and how Augustus would have reacted when he found out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think when he found out he'd wake up from torpor and march straight into the shadowlands with a bone to pick... kinda like he did do...<br /> <br /> @theGentlemanGamer I was so hoping someone would get the reference. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8150,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","user":"Talvas","date":". 01-30-2019, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T10:17:35-08:00","id":1283743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283620#post1283620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The etymology of \u201cDis\u201d is hardly certain...</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was so people would know which Pater you were talking about. Which Pater? <i>Dis </i>Pater!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll show myself out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T10:19:53-08:00","id":1283744,"title":"","content":"I think that's only for the Long Island/New Jersey branch of the Giovanni family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T14:46:19-08:00","id":1283800,"title":"","content":"So many paters, so little worship time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T09:58:54-08:00","id":1283955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283131#post1283131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind not all the Giovanni are working for the Endless Night. Augustus is, and he ultimately commands the clan, but the list of those &quot;in the known&quot; is very short indeed and a few of those are actually trying to prevent Augustus from suceeding, among them Ambrogino Giovanni. Most Giovanni ancillae and neonates don't even believe Augustus exists!.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the impression I got from the Clanbook. Everything I've read there seems to suggest the ritual is common knowledge among Clan members. Not surprising considering what a huge (and visible to necromancers) undertaking gathering all those souls is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T19:28:32-08:00","id":1284436,"title":"","content":"Most below I'd say 8th gen just know that they tithe, souls or money. But of course a better, or older necromancer who is 9th-13th might know all about it. <br /> <br /> The lesser families were given a refresher on Necromancy and are pissed about it, so they probably don't know as a whole.<br /> <br /> But I leave it up to my character, he is working towards it. I once had one who just tithed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T16:15:05-08:00","id":1284825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283568#post1283568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just another mask worn by Cappadocius, maybe? I like the idea the Giovanni were worshipping him even before they knew about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>From reading Clanbook: Cappadocians and Setite, IF manipulation was involved it seems to me Dis Pater could be the alias for a setite. Lazarus was linked to Setites as he hid in Egypth and did not heed Capadocius' call for tyhe feast of Folly. Later he supposedly was able to kill his eldest brother Kaias because he resorted to Serpentis. He's strongly hinted to be the being hiding behind the Capuchin, and it's more than likely the Capuchin helped Augustus Giovanni carry his plans on. Dis Pater was also mentioned as one of the &quot;deities&quot; used by setites for their cults.<br /> <br /> That said, in my chronicle of ages Dis Pater is exactly what he's supposed to be, a very powerful, very old wraith. He's been manipulating the Giovanni since Roman times and he allied with Lazarus helping him carry on his plan in exchange for Lazarus' help gaining access to Enoch (in the Shadowlands). I also had Lazarus betray Cappadocius not because of setite manipulation but because he was trying to foil Lilith's plan for Cappadocius, diablerizing God, which was exactly what Lilith wanted and the reason why she led Lazarus to embrace Lamia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T16:20:31-08:00","id":1284829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283955#post1283955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the impression I got from the Clanbook. Everything I've read there seems to suggest the ritual is common knowledge among Clan members. Not surprising considering what a huge (and visible to necromancers) undertaking gathering all those souls is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The clanbook is written with the PoV of 2 Giovanni who are in the known, but it's also stated (now, I remember reading this but not exactly where, sorry for that) that the younger generations of Giovanni vampires don't believe Augustus exists and even mock the &quot;legend&quot; calling him &quot;Uncle Augie&quot;. Besides, so many Giovanni knowing the clan is working to cause ghost apocalypse does not make sense. The other clans and sects would never accept that and would destroy them and it would be pratically impossible to keep the information secret (the first Giovanni neonate to be dominated would spill everything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T12:47:40-08:00","id":1285987,"title":"","content":"My headcanon has always been that Dis Pater is Set. An identity he used in the shadowlands, and which he moved into permanently after being slain. The Giovannis quick advances in Necromancy, catching the eye os the Cappadocians, the coup and purge of the Capps... all Sets strike against Cappadocious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T00:48:10-07:00","id":1321129,"title":"","content":"A bit of thread necromancy going on here... perhaps appropriately.<br /> <br /> First let me say that my idea is tangled in terms of game mechanics - but we are dealing with antediluvians, so that is par for the course. Also, I doubt there is a real and secret White Wolf / Onyx Path plan for Dis Pater. The writers generally introduce plot elements as mysteries and question marks, and rely on the gamers to answer the question and solve the mystery on their own.<br /> <br /> That said, what if Dis Pater (a patron of the Giovanni) is Cappadocius?<br /> <br /> The background for Cappadocius reads that his embrace went wrong in some manner, and that upon death he lost some part of himself in the underworld. He apparently spent the rest of his existence try to get that part back, and it also drove his questing obsession with death.<br /> <br /> What if Dis Pater is the portion of the soul Cappadocius \u201clost\u201d upon his embrace?<br /> <br /> In Wraith terms, it might be his shadow \u2013 which would have been created upon his transformation into a wraith, but he might have regarded it as \u201clost\u201d when he became a vampire. This would mean he was a vampire \u2013 an antediluvian no less \u2013 with both a shadow and a beast. This is not that exceptional; Tzimisce allegedly has two beasts.<br /> <br /> In any case, in this Dis Pater is the manifestation of all of Cappadocius worst traits. Also, a wraith shadow never stops whispering poison, and bad ideas, into a the ear of the wraith. Bad ideas such as \u201cembrace Augustus\u201d and \u201cyou can become God if you do X, Y and Z.\u201d<br /> <br /> This would also explain why it \u201cguided\u201d the Giovanni to destroying the Cappadocians; the shadow of a wraith hates the wraith and seeks to dominate it, or even its destruction. It would also explain why Dis Pater is \u201cguiding\u201d the Giovanni to try and destroy the shroud \u2013 it possesses a nihilistic version of Cappadocius own obsession with the shadowlands and death.<br /> <br /> This, I think, make the fate of Cappadocius and his clan less dumb \u2013 they did not fall victim simply to his stupidity, but to the 10,000 year old manifestation of all his malice, and death-worshiping aspects.<br /> <br /> It also means the independence and power of the Giovanni is largely an illusion \u2013 they are still in service to Cappadocius, after a fashion. To take it a step further, the lost bit of blood Cappadocius\u2019s might be his final fetter, meaning this shadow could still manifest in the Shadowlands.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T04:10:22-07:00","id":1321145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1284825#post1284825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From reading Clanbook: Cappadocians and Setite, IF manipulation was involved it seems to me Dis Pater could be the alias for a setite. Lazarus was linked to Setites as he hid in Egypth and did not heed Capadocius' call for tyhe feast of Folly. Later he supposedly was able to kill his eldest brother Kaias because he resorted to Serpentis. He's strongly hinted to be the being hiding behind the Capuchin, and it's more than likely the Capuchin helped Augustus Giovanni carry his plans on. Dis Pater was also mentioned as one of the &quot;deities&quot; used by setites for their cults.<br /> <br /> That said, in my chronicle of ages Dis Pater is exactly what he's supposed to be, a very powerful, very old wraith. He's been manipulating the Giovanni since Roman times and he allied with Lazarus helping him carry on his plan in exchange for Lazarus' help gaining access to Enoch (in the Shadowlands). I also had Lazarus betray Cappadocius not because of setite manipulation but because he was trying to foil Lilith's plan for Cappadocius, diablerizing God, which was exactly what Lilith wanted and the reason why she led Lazarus to embrace Lamia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wish we had Wraith powers to represent Godlike Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Buuut we do have Onceborn, wraith/specters growing to godhood.... So I say Dis Pater may have been an Old Wraith, who became a Specter, developed a cult and ate enough souls to become a demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T13:51:07-07:00","id":1321244,"title":"","content":"is it wrong that I read the title of this thread as Arnold Schwarzenegger?<br /> <br /> &quot;Who is Dis Pater... and what does he do?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm<br /> Kingdoms of the Shattered Crown (D&amp;D 5e) Bi Weekly Thur 7:30pm<br /> <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming</a> (all listings are AZ time: PST/MST)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","name":"Sycophant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T23:32:04-07:00","id":1321344,"title":"","content":"&quot;Who es Dis Pater... and whaat does he doo?&quot;<br /> <br /> Heh.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the Blood Gods book will offer any insight on the official story of Dis Pater, or his involvement with the Johns. I mean, I doubt my theory above will be what they go with, but some info on the current relationship would be interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T17:33:06-07:00","id":1321443,"title":"","content":"Now who thinks Augustus was a Sorcerer and who thinks he was a Mage. In Giovanni revised there are lots of clues that the endless night shroud removal ritual was actually Cappy\u2019s idea and they don\u2019t even know they are following his plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T21:04:22-07:00","id":1321457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1283601#post1283601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Cult of Typhon, as you see, survived in a fex places, celebrating the rites of Bacchus, Pluto and Mars. Even some cult groups persisted witout any vampire to lead them. For Example, a letter from a Setite of Venice of the tenth century mentions acult of Pluto all-mortal called the Skiathos of Dis, led by a family named DiGiovanni.&quot;<br /> <br /> -Clanbook: Setite revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting news to me.<br /> <br /> However, it doesn't strike me as right that the Giovanni are simply being manipulated by the Setites. Although it would make an interesting Jyhad-level secret for PCs to learn in one chronicle. But as the canon &quot;truth&quot; I am uneasy with it.<br /> <br /> My personal preference is that the Giovanni are ultimately being manipulated by a Malfean.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T21:10:25-07:00","id":1321458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321129#post1321129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, in this Dis Pater is the manifestation of all of Cappadocius worst traits. Also, a wraith shadow never stops whispering poison, and bad ideas, into a the ear of the wraith. Bad ideas such as \u201cembrace Augustus\u201d and \u201cyou can become God if you do X, Y and Z.\u201d<br /> <br /> This would also explain why it \u201cguided\u201d the Giovanni to destroying the Cappadocians; the shadow of a wraith hates the wraith and seeks to dominate it, or even its destruction. It would also explain why Dis Pater is \u201cguiding\u201d the Giovanni to try and destroy the shroud \u2013 it possesses a nihilistic version of Cappadocius own obsession with the shadowlands and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>An intriguing idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T13:21:13-07:00","id":1321533,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I've thought for some time the end of Cappadocius, and his clan, was weak-sauce, and my theory does improve on that story. But it is one of those abstract ideas - it looks good on paper, but how would you make it real and meaningful in a VtM game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T18:16:12-07:00","id":1321676,"title":"","content":"The reason I guessed that Dis Pater is or was an alias of Set is that the whole thing was very Setite. Tempt the original merchant family with riches, then give them secrets of necromancy that would tempt an Antediluvian into lowering his caution. (And those much have been deep and valuable secrets no matter who Dis Pater was. Hoarding such things for temptation is very Setite.)<br /> <br /> Then Cappadocious embraces Augustus, but not in person. His vitae is carried in a jar to the waiting Augustus -by Lazarus!, who at this point was totally compromised by the Setites. And who were said to have done some mystical stuff to it. And who then keeps Augustus mortal blood in the jar and it vanishes. Its so Setite. Tempt, tempt again, have a Setite agent manage the embrace, and then keep a bodypart as security. Similar to a heart but not quite. And it all ends up with the destruction of an Antediluvian strongly opposed to Set. And his replacement by a new Ante probably under the control of the Setites, desperately chasing the True Vessel with his mortal blood in.<br /> <br /> So if the shroud comes down, whats going to happen to Osiris, Duat and all the mummies there? Anything good? Don't think so somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T07:22:38-07:00","id":1321713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321676#post1321676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I guessed that Dis Pater is or was an alias of Set is that the whole thing was very Setite. Tempt the original merchant family with riches, then give them secrets of necromancy that would tempt an Antediluvian into lowering his caution. (And those much have been deep and valuable secrets no matter who Dis Pater was. Hoarding such things for temptation is very Setite.)<br /> <br /> Then Cappadocious embraces Augustus, but not in person. His vitae is carried in a jar to the waiting Augustus -by Lazarus!, who at this point was totally compromised by the Setites. And who were said to have done some mystical stuff to it. And who then keeps Augustus mortal blood in the jar and it vanishes. Its so Setite. Tempt, tempt again, have a Setite agent manage the embrace, and then keep a bodypart as security. Similar to a heart but not quite. And it all ends up with the destruction of an Antediluvian strongly opposed to Set. And his replacement by a new Ante probably under the control of the Setites, desperately chasing the True Vessel with his mortal blood in.<br /> <br /> So if the shroud comes down, whats going to happen to Osiris, Duat and all the mummies there? Anything good? Don't think so somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with that is that Dis Pater can be summoned by almost any Giovanni at any time, and has weight with the Hierarchy. And vast knowledge of their traditions.<br /> <br /> I've considered the mage angle, but I like Grumpy's best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T07:25:18-07:00","id":1321715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321129#post1321129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of thread necromancy going on here... perhaps appropriately.<br /> <br /> First let me say that my idea is tangled in terms of game mechanics - but we are dealing with antediluvians, so that is par for the course. Also, I doubt there is a real and secret White Wolf / Onyx Path plan for Dis Pater. The writers generally introduce plot elements as mysteries and question marks, and rely on the gamers to answer the question and solve the mystery on their own.<br /> <br /> That said, what if Dis Pater (a patron of the Giovanni) is Cappadocius?<br /> <br /> The background for Cappadocius reads that his embrace went wrong in some manner, and that upon death he lost some part of himself in the underworld. He apparently spent the rest of his existence try to get that part back, and it also drove his questing obsession with death.<br /> <br /> What if Dis Pater is the portion of the soul Cappadocius \u201clost\u201d upon his embrace?<br /> <br /> In Wraith terms, it might be his shadow \u2013 which would have been created upon his transformation into a wraith, but he might have regarded it as \u201clost\u201d when he became a vampire. This would mean he was a vampire \u2013 an antediluvian no less \u2013 with both a shadow and a beast. This is not that exceptional; Tzimisce allegedly has two beasts.<br /> <br /> In any case, in this Dis Pater is the manifestation of all of Cappadocius worst traits. Also, a wraith shadow never stops whispering poison, and bad ideas, into a the ear of the wraith. Bad ideas such as \u201cembrace Augustus\u201d and \u201cyou can become God if you do X, Y and Z.\u201d<br /> <br /> This would also explain why it \u201cguided\u201d the Giovanni to destroying the Cappadocians; the shadow of a wraith hates the wraith and seeks to dominate it, or even its destruction. It would also explain why Dis Pater is \u201cguiding\u201d the Giovanni to try and destroy the shroud \u2013 it possesses a nihilistic version of Cappadocius own obsession with the shadowlands and death.<br /> <br /> This, I think, make the fate of Cappadocius and his clan less dumb \u2013 they did not fall victim simply to his stupidity, but to the 10,000 year old manifestation of all his malice, and death-worshiping aspects.<br /> <br /> It also means the independence and power of the Giovanni is largely an illusion \u2013 they are still in service to Cappadocius, after a fashion. To take it a step further, the lost bit of blood Cappadocius\u2019s might be his final fetter, meaning this shadow could still manifest in the Shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one that makes the most sense so far, to me at least. The Set angle is, like a really really long con for what profit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T07:27:16-07:00","id":1321716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sycophant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321244#post1321244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it wrong that I read the title of this thread as Arnold Schwarzenegger?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Who is Dis Pater... and what does he do?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be wrong if you didn't read it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T08:28:53-07:00","id":1321725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321676#post1321676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the shroud comes down, whats going to happen to Osiris, Duat and all the mummies there? Anything good? Don't think so somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That would be the complete end for the Reborn. Do not pass go. Do not resurrect. They also would have no way to stop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T16:31:08-07:00","id":1321790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talvas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321713#post1321713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only problem with that is that Dis Pater can be summoned by almost any Giovanni at any time, and has weight with the Hierarchy. And vast knowledge of their traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the bit about Dis Pater being summonable by any Giovanni?<br /> <br /> As far as knowledge and influence goes, its not beyond an Antediluvian with Bane Mummies. There is also the notion that Set was slain by Osiris around the time of Christ or so, at which point he would have become a wraith semipermanently. The thing with the Setites is, though, that they have been feuding with the mummies for ten thousand years, and some of that have been afterlife based.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talvas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321715#post1321715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Set angle is, like a really really long con for what profit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh...what? They got to take down an actual Antediluvian hostile to Set. Thats a huge Jyhad win, of the sort that doesn't come around every millennium. They also got to nearly exterminate a rival clan. And Uncle Auggie is not really a player on the level of the true Antes in the Jyhad. If they are influencing him to tear down the shroud... the got a member of the Third Generation and his clan on the hook. I cant really see how any possible payout, short of an outright Jyhad win, could be bigger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 07-01-2019, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T23:04:51-07:00","id":1321835,"title":"","content":"I don't think Dis Pater got Cappy Eaten, Cappy got Cappy Eaten.<br /> <br /> And its not a sure thing Set was killed by Osiris at the time of Christ, he just disappeared at that time and there was a lot of omens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T00:52:34-07:00","id":1321853,"title":"","content":"Dis Pater, in this theory, is Cappadocius - simply his shadow side. So, Dis Pater destroying Cappadocius is still Cappadocius arranging the destruction of Cappadocius.<br /> <br /> Edit: It would be interesting if Augustus had at some point learned, or realized, what was happening and this is part fuels his dangerous desperation.<br /> <br /> I think this also gives an interesting color to the Harbringer's vendetta against the Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Dis Tater - a ghostly spud - made me do it. 07-02-2019, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T10:49:36-07:00","id":1321891,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else keep the ghost of Cappy around and not have him dead due to the Maelstrom, which I think is anticlimactic that the death of one Ante is so potent and causes so much collateral it kills the ghost of another?<br /> <br /> I think my head Canon will be Cappadocius performed a transubstantiation of his soul into a Neverborn when Augustus Ate him, making him a Onceborn. And he has been pulling the strings of the final night ritual so he can eat a million Souls and Ascend to a high enough state to attempt to seize the throne of God. The Giovanni meanwhile have no idea and are walking to their doom.<br /> <br /> Also any idea in what ways Augustus is weaker because he never ate Cappy\u2019s soul? What about the idea he never obtained 3rd generation but it warped his blood enough to create the Giovanni, and he is secretly 4th gen? Who are his stated childer in the Books? Does he have any pre-bite childer to compare to the post bite ones? The curse made it so other premascines would be able to only embrace Giovanni right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T11:24:57-07:00","id":1321900,"title":"","content":"That whatever is left of Cappadocius - wraith or spectre - finessed his way into becoming a Onceborn would work mechanically, and be more interesting than him fading away or something so (you are right) anticlimactic. That he intended to eat those 100 million souls is also a solid idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T18:42:59-07:00","id":1321947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321790#post1321790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is the bit about Dis Pater being summonable by any Giovanni?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in the revised clanbook. On page 17 under Dis Pater, that reverence of him goes so far back and is so ingrained that any member of the family may call on him and if the need great enough he will respond.<br /> <br /> I took that mechanically to be that with Sepulchre 3 and knowing the name Dis Pater, you could summon him but if the need is not great enough he'll kill you.<br /> <br /> Or at the very least this entity can hear most Giovanni and is not Set listening in to keep a long con going and showing up to aid Giovanni Necromancers against whatever stuff they got themselves into, like the wraith Hierarchy etc.<br /> <br /> Could Set even do all of that? And why do it for Gios but not his own Setites?<br /> <br /> Edit: That would also make clan Gio more successful at worshipping Set than Setites are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8150,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","user":"Talvas","date":". 07-02-2019, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T18:57:04-07:00","id":1321950,"title":"","content":"What I don't understand is how, knowing that Specters have a hive mind, how they haven't figured out what the Giovanni are planning for the shroud and joined in to help. <br /> <br /> It seems like smashing the shroud and joining the two, if they could somehow make sure another maelstrom comes, could break the whole thing and tear through, finally unleashing Oblivion or whatever it is that's down there. My actual wraith knowledge is limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T19:08:28-07:00","id":1321953,"title":"","content":"Man I always hated Specters being all Hivemind Buddies, one of the big reasons I would imagine Wraiths becoming specters would be to harm specters that ruined everything for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhooo I am actually more curious as to the providence of Baron Samedi then Dis Pater. At one point I entertained the notion Samedi was Cappadocius, and that isn't out of the question even now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T21:42:27-07:00","id":1321973,"title":"","content":"I'd have to dig my copy of Spectres out to look, but I think I recall Hive Mind requiring a fair amount of skill to pick useful information out of the din and confusion of countless voices of nihilism, self hatred, and destructive impulse all talking at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T21:56:08-07:00","id":1322156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1321973#post1321973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to dig my copy of Spectres out to look, but I think I recall Hive Mind requiring a fair amount of skill to pick useful information out of the din and confusion of countless voices of nihilism, self hatred, and destructive impulse all talking at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but I mean the fact that Spectres come in waves, rather then what you would expect that they wouldn't be able to handle the sight of themselves or each other. But the book portrayed it they all worked together, but when alone in the Labyrinthe they sometimes eat each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T17:40:55-07:00","id":1324837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282780-who-is-dis-pater-and-what-does-he-do?p=1322156#post1322156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but I mean the fact that Spectres come in waves, rather then what you would expect that they wouldn't be able to handle the sight of themselves or each other. But the book portrayed it they all worked together, but when alone in the Labyrinthe they sometimes eat each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the clanbook they are portrayed that way sort of. If you hurt one up to three more can show up and have an equal chance to attack the Necromancer or the specter he summoned that was wounded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8150-talvas","name":"Talvas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T09:48:06-07:00","id":1451146,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Within my own chronicle, Dis Pater is in fact a powerful Fallen of the Halaku House who served under Azrael. Upon his escape, Dis Pater (whose celestial name was Gadreel) found refuge within the Spirit-Realm under the guise of a powerful wraith and there founded the city of Dis, wherein he lured the Ferrymen to take residence. Later he taught the ambitious Giovanni the art of necromancy while secretly using the necromancers as both a source of faith and as pawns to further his own agenda. A master deceiver and manipulator, he pulls the strings of multiple groups to further his own agenda. One such deception being the great lie of the Endless Night which he fed to Agustus in order to have the Giovanni bring down the Shroud. Upon the merging of the two realms Dis Pater/Gadreel will then create a new Heaven according to his own design.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Gadreel - The Fourth Fallen Angel</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#54555E\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">God banished Gadreel from heaven. His sin was to teach man of death...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":19671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19671-dgs-chad","user":"DGS-Chad","date":". 06-06-2021, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19671-dgs-chad","name":"DGS-Chad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T11:52:32-07:00","id":1451155,"title":"","content":"As a side note, and sorry if it was already answered, but Caesar said that Dis Pater (that is, a divinity sharing many traits with Dis) was the &quot;father God&quot; of the Gauls, who believed that when they died, their souls returned to him and then he sent them back to life.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it can be of interest or help in the Masquarade settings, but I guess it can allow for some tricks, certainly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T17:23:35-07:00","id":1451173,"title":"","content":"&quot;So it's been years since I wrote the Judgment scenario for the old Mage. Due to space considerations and not wanting to territorially pee on other people's games and the other game lines, there were several things I left out. Some things were cut. Some things were implied. Some things I used as working assumptions. Since none of that matters much any more, here's as much of that stuff as I can remember, in point form. Note that none of it was canon, in that it did not pass developmental consensus or anything. It is purely what went into writing Judgment. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Giovanni, the Orphic Circle and all the other factions in the World of Darkness who use necromancy and inevitably decide that its ultimate goal is to tear the shroud down, do that because Voormas memetically poisoned necromancy ages ago to help wreck the cycle. (And you thought Intellectual Entropy was useless, didn't you!) Incidentally, if that Etruscan Lich had gained any social traction it probably could have pointed this out.&quot;<br /> <br /> - excerpts from the LiveJournal of writer Malcom Sheppard, <a href=\"https://eyebeams.livejournal.com/396330.html?\" target=\"_blank\">https://eyebeams.livejournal.com/396330.html?</a><br /> <br /> What the author is saying here is that, in his headcanon, one of the archvillains of the M:tA game line used his influence over what death magic means to make tearing down the shroud the end goal of every sufficiently advanced necromancer. The idea of tearing down the shroud is attributable to this one guy. <br /> <br /> (Voormas had his own scheme to break the Wheel of Ages and become something like the Demon Emperor, and breaking death was an essential part of the plan.)<br /> <br /> I know embarrassingly little about the lore of the M:tA line, but find it fascinating how little that part of the WoD comes up when we talk about magical shenanigans in Vampire.<br /> <br /> Somebody who knows more might be able to take Sheppard's idea, quoted above, and the Tal'mahe'ra's roots in the Euthanatoi and run for miles with it for all I know. What I do know, from what little got published over the years on the True Black Hand, is that the Chakravanti mages who became the Nagaraja hate the Setites' guts, and that they took on the vampriric curse themselves as the karmic price for stewardship over Enoch precisely because the city's guardian Mummy warned them that otherwise the city would fall into the hands of the Setites and that would be bad.<br /> <br /> I love how complex some of these really marginal subplots get. Threads like this are a joy to me. Kudos to everyone contributing their ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 06-06-2021, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}